      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that both $2a$ and $-\\frac{2}{3}a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $2a$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\nNext, for the vector $-\\frac{2}{3}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{2}{3}a$ is $\\frac{2}{3}$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{2}{3}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{2}{3}$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](generate/scratch/17592186096649-draft/plots/8ba0180ca04cb3be3ae1299bfab95fddb1ec4e1d3cf64438a338f5ec87665216.png)"
